WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.485 --> 00:00:03.068
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.900
- Hi, everyone, my name is Jesse,

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.240
and I'm an educator here
at the Peabody Museum.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.628
Today, we're gonna be making
a butterfly ring or bracelet.

00:00:12.628 --> 00:00:15.330
(silence)

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.080
So this is a very simple
activity that you can do at home.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.070
For this, you'll need to have some paper.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:24.220
You can use construction
paper or recycled paper.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.620
You'll need something to draw with.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.660
You can use a pen or a
pencil, crayons, or markers

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.000
if you have them,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.273
some tape, and some scissors.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.380
So let's get started.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.730
So for this activity,

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.680
you can look at butterflies
in your backyard,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.290
you can watch a video that
we posted from entomology

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.970
and check out some of the butterflies

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.510
that live in the tropics,

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:51.600
or you can look one up online or in a book

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.300
to decide what you'd like to draw.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.700
I'm gonna just use my imagination today.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.940
So the way you get started,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.317
you're gonna draw a B
shape onto your paper...

00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:05.090
(silence)

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.440
Just like that, just to get started.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.900
It's okay if it doesn't look
exactly like a butterfly.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.410
You're gonna take your folded paper

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.832
and cut out along the shape.

00:01:15.832 --> 00:01:18.832
(scissors snipping)

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.813
Now we have the beginnings of
our sweet little butterfly.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.060
So now you can color it in.

00:01:36.432 --> 00:01:40.099
(crayon lightly scratching)

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.510
When you're happy with your drawing,

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:14.650
now we're gonna make the ring
for our ring or our bracelet.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.700
So you can take the paper
that you cut out earlier,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.410
and you're just gonna cut
a small strip of paper

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.967
off the top.

00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:24.967
(scissors snipping)

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.240
And for this part, you
might need to ask a grownup

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.390
for some help to get it the right size

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.840
to be able to put it on
your hand or your wrist.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.980
So when you have your piece of paper,

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.450
you're gonna fold it over onto itself

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.960
to make a little ring just like that.

00:02:41.805 --> 00:02:43.910
(tape ripping)

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.840
You can take a piece of tape and stick it

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.060
onto the part where the ring closes,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.750
and then you're gonna fold
the tape into the ring

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:56.143
to close it so you can
see it just like that.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.550
This one's kind of small; I
think it'll fit on my finger.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.640
So before you put it on,

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.640
you wanna take another piece of tape...

00:03:06.804 --> 00:03:07.700
(tape ripping)

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.533
We're gonna create a second ring.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:16.130
So take one edge, fold it
over, and stick it onto itself,

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.150
and you're gonna take your tape ring

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.143
and put it right onto your paper ring.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:28.870
Now we can put our butterfly
on, and it will be ready to go.

00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:35.280
There you go; great job, everyone.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.830
Feel free to send us pictures
of the ones you make.

00:03:38.705 --> 00:03:41.288
(bright music)

